WEBVTT

00:48:29.208 --> 00:48:34.226
I think there's beauty and value
in each of these models.

00:48:34.250 --> 00:48:37.726
But everyone has a clear sense
of what they were told growing up.

00:48:37.750 --> 00:48:41.934
I really do think it's
a real foundational set of messages

00:48:41.958 --> 00:48:44.583
that shape our relational legacy.

00:48:45.458 --> 00:48:48.309
AG: There are a couple other
quick things I wanted to raise.

00:48:48.333 --> 00:48:51.851
One is from Susan Dominus.
So we share something very unusual.

00:48:51.875 --> 00:48:53.559
EP: Yes, I have to explain that.

00:48:53.583 --> 00:48:55.893
I mean, basically,
Susan Dominus is a journalist

00:48:55.917 --> 00:48:57.226
at "The New York Times"

00:48:57.250 --> 00:49:00.559
and she wrote a profile about me
and she wrote a profile about Adam.